// Portable runtime semantics implemented in Abla and compiled into the same
// LLVM unit as the application. Typed scalar expressions lower through the
// compiler's normal scalar path; the functions below handle boxed/dynamic
// values at the universal-value ABI boundary.

// These are the irreducible value-layout and raw-memory operations used by
// the runtime below. They are the temporary boundary until Abla has an
// unboxed tagged-union/record representation. Collection, strings, arrays,
// objects, arithmetic, comparisons, and ownership policy are ordinary Abla.
